<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Wheat bids lower.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Wheat bids lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring bids were mostly lower on Thursday as dealers noted some grain coming into elevators in several parts of the Northern Plains states.</p>
<p>There were a few more cars on the floor, which knocked down the basis, a Minneapolis dealer said.</p>
<p>USDA's Market News Service said 359 cars and 10 trains of spring wheat were received on the Minneapolis cash trading floor on Thursday.</p>
<p>MGE spring wheat futures closed mixed, with nearby March and May weak on evidence of increased wheat moving from the country, traders said. MGE March wheat lost 1-3/4 cents to end at $3.87-1/2.  </p>
